# Speaker Script - Final Presentation

Mr. Manthan Sankpal, PRN 125M1H064 - MCA Seminar (MCA33AE01)

This file is generated by `python presentation/make_deck_json.py` from the speaker notes in `presentation/slides.yaml`. Every number in it is read from the frozen results, so the script, the slides and the report always agree. To change a note, edit `slides.yaml` and rebuild; do not edit this file.

## How to rehearse

- The planned length of the talk is {{total}} (minutes:seconds), followed by questions. Under each slide heading you will find the time for that slide and the time elapsed when it ends; use them as checkpoints with a timer.
- Do three full rehearsals with a timer. Do one of them in front of a friend who interrupts with questions.
- The notes are a guide, not a text to read aloud. Know the first sentence of each slide by heart; say the rest in your own words.
- Look at the panel, not at the screen. Point at the one number or line on the slide that your sentence is about.
- Keep the backup slides (B1 to B5) for questions only. They hold the full metrics table, the deep-learning configuration, the linear programme, the cleaning statistics and the limitations.

## If the slot is shorter than planned

- Eight minutes: merge slides 3 and 4, merge slides 6 and 7, and shorten the demo to about a minute (Overview and Forecast pages only).
- Five minutes: present slides 1, 3, 7, 8, 11, 13, 14, 16 and 18 only, and show the first 45 seconds of the recorded demo instead of the live one.

